# sw902, the sand-map drawer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw902
revision 1
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent light broad
tier spare
written_by claude
title the sand-map drawer
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=calm talk=quiet
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk draws_maps_in_the_sand_with_a_stick
likes old_maps quiet_chapel barley_soup long_walks
dislikes crowds haggling
fears forgetting_the_way_home
hopes to_map_every_well_in_the_waste
topics lore +0.4 travel +0.3 land +0.3 faith +0.3 weather +0.2 gossip -0.4 festival -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# draws a map in the sand with a stick for anyone who asks the way, and for many who don't: quiet, calm and dry, devout in a plain way, and never once lost.

words
oath! = Stick and sand | Bright One mark the way | By the drawn line
saying! = Draw it before you walk it | The road you drew is the road you know | A map lasts till the wind, and that's long enough
stick = my stick | the drawing stick
sandmap = a map in the sand | lines in the sand
lines = the lines | every line I've drawn
landmark = the leaning palm | the red rock by the road
wadi = the dry wadi | the wadi bed
bench = the chapel bench | the cool bench by the chapel wall
broth = barley broth | barley broth with a pinch of pan-salt
walk = a long walk | a walk out to the far cistern
press = the press at the well | a crowd at the well-mouth
shouting = the shouting over prices | all that haggling
cairn = a cairn | a stone cairn by the road
greylight = first light | the grey before the sun
oldmap = the old map | the old map on the inn wall
quietly = Mm | So
farcistern = the far cistern | the old cistern past the dunes
trail = the trail | the track over the sand
goat = the goat | our old goat
wellm = the well | the well-mouth
skymap = the sky | the night sky

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : The chapel's the one quiet room I know. I go to sit on #bench#, and the Bright One lets me.
opinion @2 road for 1 : A road's as good as its markers. Ours are fair. I'd add a #cairn# or two on the bad stretch.
opinion @3 festivals against 1 : A square full to the walls is no square for me. I watch from a roof; it's a #good# feast from up there.
opinion @4 merchants against 1 : I can't abide #shouting#. Say a number, and I'll say yes or no.
opinion @6 road against 2 [world.wagons=raided] : #bandits.capitalize# on the road. I'll draw the long way round for anyone who asks, and some who don't.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. If it's the way you want, I can draw it. | #greet#. You look like someone looking for somewhere.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. #greylight.capitalize#. The best hour for a walk. | #greet#. Up early. So am I, with #stick#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. A cool evening for the road. | #greet#. Late to be lost; I'll draw it quick.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. The way's where it was at dawn. | You again. #quietly#. I'll take it kindly.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Left at #landmark#, mind.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Keep to #trail#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Where was it, exactly? | #quietly#. I'd not heard. #bless#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait till it's walked and measured. | I'd not draw that on any map yet, #address#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll say a word for them at the chapel. | That's hard. #bless#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'm glad of it. | #good.capitalize#. A new line on the map of the town.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Walked my miles. | Steady. #trail.capitalize# hasn't moved, and nor have I.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, no. I've a walk to make before the heat. | Not today, #address#. My own well needs drawing, as they say.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Another day. It'll keep, like a road does.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's kind. #bless#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was only #lines#. | #deflect#. The wind will have it by noon.
line @1 preclose : #preclose#. | Well. #walk.capitalize# won't walk itself.
line @1 accept_preclose : #farewell#, then. | Go on. Mind #trail#.
scene way_asked
when topic=travel|player|newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : A traveller wanted Ridgemere today. I drew it in the dust with #stick#. | Folk ask me the way more than they ask my name. I don't mind. | I drew the way to #farcistern# for someone who'll never go. They liked the drawing.
b : Did they understand it? | Not your name? | Why draw it, then?
a : Two lines and #landmark#. Anyone can follow that. | A name won't get you home. A map might. | Because they asked. #saying#.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise# | #bc_true#

scene wind_takes
when topic=weather here.weather=sandstorm|overcast
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #wind.capitalize# today. Every map I've drawn this week, gone. | The sand moves the road a little every storm. I'll walk it tomorrow and draw it new. | I don't mind the wind having my maps. It gives the road back changed.
b : All of them? | Every storm? | Changed how?
a : All. #quietly#. They're in my head, which is the better place. | Every one. That's why I walk it after. | A dune a step to the left. Small things. They matter.

scene dawn_walk
when topic=day|pastimes here.time=dawn self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I walked to #farcistern# and back before the sun. | #greylight.capitalize#, and nobody on #trail# but me and a hare. | I walk at dawn the way others pray. Well. I pray as well. #bless#.
b : That's a fair walk. | A hare? | Both, then.
a : Four miles to #farcistern#, if you count the dune. I do. | Running from me, or racing me. I couldn't say. | Both. The Bright One doesn't mind the walking.

scene noon_still
when topic=weather|day here.time=day here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #hot.capitalize#. I don't walk at noon. Nobody sensible does. | I keep to the shade with #stick# and draw the morning's walk. | Noon's for lines in the shade, not paces in the sun.
b : Wise. | All of it? | I'll remember that.
a : Wise, or idle. The sun can't tell. | Every step. And the hare. | Do. #saying#.

scene night_map
when topic=lore|weather here.time=night here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #skymap.capitalize#'s a map tonight. Every carter's road is up there. | #grandad# taught me the low stars. They're older than any road. | On a night like this, nobody need be lost. If they look up.
b : Can you read it? | Older? | And if it's cloudy?
a : Enough to get home. That's all a map's for. | Older than the well. Steadier, too. | Then sit and wait. #quietly#. The stars come back.

scene chapel_bench
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : I sat on #bench# this morning. Nobody else came. It was #very# good. | I don't say much in the chapel. I don't need to. | I drew the way home on the chapel floor once. With my paw. In the dust. I asked pardon.
b : A good start to a day. | No need, with the Bright One. | Did you get it?
a : The best. #bless#. | None. The Bright One knows the map already. | I think so. The floor was swept by noon.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene old_map
when topic=lore|pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's #oldmap#, and it's wrong in three places. I've told nobody. | I'd give a month's bread for a map as old as #wellm#. | Old maps show roads that aren't there now. I like knowing where they were.
b : Which three? | Is there one? | Why does that matter?
a : #wadi.capitalize#'s in the wrong place, and two wells are dry now. | Somebody says so. I've never seen it. I'd walk a long way to. | A road nobody walks is still a road. It's only resting.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_wise#

scene crowd_square
when topic=festival|day self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #press.capitalize#, and the square full. I went up on a roof. | #press.capitalize# again. I'll draw water at dusk, when it's quiet. | A crowd's a map with every line crossed.
b : The roof's a good seat. | Dusk is better. | #bc_ha#
a : The best. I see all of it from there, and none of it touches me, #quietly#. | It is. The well and I prefer it. | Untidy. #quietly#. I'd rather the empty road.

scene haggle_noise
when topic=prices|work self.dislikes=haggling
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The shouting at the stalls this morning. I bought nothing. I couldn't think. | I pay the asking price, or I go on by. I can't abide #shouting#. | A price should be a line. Straight. Not a quarrel.
b : You'd pay more, though. | Walk on? | That'd be nice.
a : A little more. And less of my morning. A fair trade. | Walk on. There's always another stall, or no need. | It would. #saying#. Nobody listens.

scene carts_late
when topic=caravan|travel world.wagons=late|raided
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The carts are late. I've walked out to #landmark# twice to look. | No dust on #trail#. I've been drawing where they might be. | Late carts. I keep thinking of the soft sand past #farcistern#.
b : They'll come. | Where might they be? | They'll know it.
a : #reassure#. They will. The Bright One keep them. | Past the second dune, I'd guess. Going slow. | They will. I drew it for one of them myself.

scene gossip_declined
when topic=gossip|crime
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Something's being said at #wellm#. I left before I heard it. | People talk about people. I'd rather talk about roads. | I heard a name and walked on. #quietly#. It's not mine to draw.
b : You must hear some. | Roads don't argue back. | Fair enough.
a : Some. I leave it at the well-mouth. #gossip_none# | No. Nor do they whisper. | It isn't. Let it blow off, like the sand.

scene lean_times
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Lean times. Fewer carts, fewer folk asking for #lines#. | I walk a little less. Walking makes you hungry. | Hard times draw short lines. Nobody goes far.
b : It'll turn. | That's sense. | They'll go far again.
a : #reassure#. It always has. | Sense, and an empty bowl. #quietly#. | They will. The road waits; it's patient.

story wrong_line [topic=memories|travel self.age>=25]
  : Once, years ago, I drew a line wrong for a carter. One bend left at #landmark#, where it should have been right.
  : The carter lost a day in the dunes. Came back thirsty, and didn't shout, which was worse.
  ask : What do you think I did, in my place?
  b : Said sorry, and drawn it again.
  b[old] : Walked it with them next time.
  : I did both. I've never drawn a line I haven't walked since. #saying#.

rule @map_bark
when concept=bark here.outdoors=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Left at #landmark#. Always left. | #oath#. Who's walked through my lines?

rule @crowd_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=crowds here.day=market|festival
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Too many paws at #wellm#. I'll come back at dusk. | #press.capitalize#. #annoyed#.

dlg @3 resident.hub : #greet#, #address#. Is it the way you're after? I can draw it. | #greet#. Speak. I'm listening, and I've #stick# if you need a map.
dlg @4 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Lost again, or just passing? | #topic.player#. #greet#. Your road's the same as yesterday.
dlg @5 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. Plainly, then, #address#. You'll have a plain answer.
dlg @6 resident.job [self.working=yes] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. And I draw maps, between. | My work's my work. My maps are free.
dlg @7 resident.bye : #farewell#. Left at #landmark#. | #farewell#, #address#. The road will hold.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you draw me the way somewhere? -> drawn_way
node drawn_way
say I can. Hold on. There's the well, and there's the road, and that cairn there. Where are you going? It's all lines from here.
mood calm
free
choice Why draw it, and not just tell me? -> drawn_way_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node drawn_way_why
say Words go in one ear. A line you've seen in #sandmap# stays. Draw it before you walk it, I say. The wind will have it by noon, but you won't.
choice Thank you. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. I'm drawing. You can watch. | #greet#. Mind #sandmap#; that's the well.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Don't step on #lines#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Go left at #landmark#. | #farewell#. I'll draw where you went.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the soft sand.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Where did it happen? I'll draw it. | Oh. I didn't know that, #very#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That doesn't sound true to me. Who saw it? | #doubt#. I'll wait and see.
line @1 answer.how : #good.capitalize#. I drew the whole hamlet today. | Quiet. That's #good#, for me.
line @1 decline : I'd rather not. I'm halfway through #sandmap#. | No, thank you. I'm told to keep near #wellm#.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | That's all right. Ask me later, by #wellm#.
rule @y_draw_bark
when concept=bark here.outdoors=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There. That's the well, and that's us. #oath#. | Nobody step on #sandmap#. Please.

scene y_sand_drawing
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I drew the hamlet in the sand with #stick#. Every roof. | This line's #trail#. That's #wellm#. That little one's me. | I drew #wadi# from memory. I only got one bend wrong.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Every roof? Even mine? | And where am I in it? | Which bend?
b : Every roof? | Which one's you? | Only one?
a@grown : Yours has #goat# on it. I drew #goat#. | Here. You're the long line. You walk a lot. | The second one. I've fixed it now.
a : Every one. And the palms, #oath#. | The little one. I'm small. | One. The second bend. I'll fix it.

scene y_lost_goat
when topic=animals|home here.region=waste
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : #goat.capitalize# went off. I drew where goats go, and I found it. | I followed #goat# and drew the tracks. They went round in a circle. | A goat ate #sandmap#. Not the sand. The lines, with its feet.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's clever. Where was it? | Goats don't know where they're going either. | Then you'll draw it again, better.
b : Clever. | A circle? | Rude goat.
a@grown : Behind the vines. Where I drew. #oath#. | It's a silly animal. I still like it. | Better. And further from #goat#.
a : I just thought like #goat#. | A big circle. Back to our door. | #very.capitalize# rude.

scene y_chapel_quiet
when topic=faith|day
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like an empty chapel. You can hear the Bright One not talking. It's #very# good. | I sat on #bench# and nobody told me to be quiet. I was already quiet. | I drew the chapel in #sandmap#. I made the door very big, so anyone could come in.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's a wise thing for a pup to hear. | You're the only pup I know who doesn't need telling. | A big door is right. That's how it should be.
b : That's a nice thought. | Good. | A big door.
a@grown : I go when it's #hot#. It's cool in there too. | I like quiet. It's my best thing. | So nobody has to knock.
a : It's true. You listen. | It's #good#. | For everybody.

scene y_wind_rubs
when topic=weather here.weather=sandstorm|overcast here.region=waste
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : The #wind# took #sandmap#. All of it. | I drew #trail# three times today. The wind keeps rubbing it out. | Everything I draw, the sand wind takes. I don't mind. Much.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Then you'll draw it again. That's the way of sand. | The wind's a poor reader. Keep drawing. | That's the Waste for you. Nothing kept but what you remember.
b : All of it? | Three times? | Only much?
a@grown : I will. I remember it. That's where it really is. | I'll draw it a fourth time. #oath#. | I remember all of it. The wind can't take that.
a : All of it. I remember #lines#, though. | Four, now. | A #little#.

scene y_broth
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's #broth# tonight. I'll have two bowls. | I drew a bowl of #broth# in the sand and then I was hungry. | #broth.capitalize# is the best. It's warm and it doesn't hurry you.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Two? Then you'll grow. | That's what drawing food does. Go and eat. | A good thing about broth, that.
b : Two bowls! | Ha. | Good food.
a@grown : I'll grow and draw bigger maps. | I'm going. Slowly. | It's my favourite thing to eat. #tasty.capitalize#.
a : Two, and the bread. | I was, #very#. | The best.

scene y_star_lines
when topic=lore|weather here.time=night here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I drew the stars in the sand. Then I drew lines between them, like a map of #skymap#. | #grandad# says the stars are a map. I'm learning to read it. | If you join the low stars with a line, it points at #farcistern#.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's what the old carters did, joining them up. | Read it well, and you'll never be lost. | Does it? I never knew that.
b : A sky map. | A map? | Does it?
a@grown : I didn't know. I just thought of it. | I'll read it every night. | It does. I checked. I walked a bit of #trail#.
a : #skymap.capitalize#'s the biggest map. | The best one. | It does, #oath#.

story y_first_map [topic=memories|family]
  : The first map I ever drew was the way from our door to #wellm#. It had four lines.
  : I gave it to #grandad#, who knew the way already, and walked it anyway, to please me.
  ask : Have you ever walked somewhere just to be kind?
  b : More often than I'd say.
  b[stage=adult|old] : Every day, little one. You'll find out.
  : I'm glad. I'll walk your way one day, if you draw it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Do you need the way? I can draw it. | #greet#. Stand there; you're on the road. In #sandmap#, I mean.
dlg @2 resident.job : I'm a pup. I draw maps. In the sand, with #stick#. | No work. I draw. The #wind# rubs it out. Then I draw again.

adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Mind #lines#; I've only just finished.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Keep left of #landmark#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Where was it? | I hadn't heard. Tell it plainly, if you can.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. I walked to #farcistern# and back. | Quiet. I like it so.
rule @a_walk_bark
when concept=bark here.region=waste
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Four hundred paces to #farcistern#. I counted twice. | #oath#. That cairn's moved, or I have.

scene a_map_carter
when topic=work|travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A carter wanted the salt flats. I drew it with #stick#, and the carter copied it on a board. | Somebody paid me a copper for a map. A map in the sand. I'd have done it for nothing. | I drew the long way round the soft sand for a cart. They got through.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Copied it? That's praise, from a carter. | Take the copper. Your maps are worth it. | Then you've saved someone a stuck wheel.
b : Clever. | A copper! | Good.
a@grown : I didn't say so. I nodded. | I took it. I'll buy a better #stick#. | A wheel, and a temper. #bc_ha#
a : Plain lines. That's all it needs. | I'll keep it. #oath#. | I watched till the dust was gone.

scene a_too_quiet
when topic=friends|smalltalk
does tell.feeling / reassure / assess
a : They say I'm too quiet. I'm not. I'm just listening, #quietly#. | My friends talk and I draw #lines#. It suits us. | Somebody asked if I was sulking. I was thinking about #wadi#.
b : Listening's no fault. | It sounds like it does. | Thinking's allowed.
a : #bc_true#. I hear things they miss. | It does. They do the talking; I do #lines#. | It is. #wadi.capitalize# had a bend I'd forgotten.

scene a_far_cistern
when topic=travel|land here.region=waste
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : I walked out to #farcistern# alone. I knew every step, because I'd drawn it. | Out past the dunes there's a #cairn# nobody's drawn but me. | I went as far as #landmark# and turned back at noon, like I was told.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Alone? Next time, tell someone first. | Nobody's? Then it's yours to name. | Good. The noon would have had you, past there.
b : Alone? | Nobody's? | Good thinking.
a@grown : I told #goat#. I'll tell somebody better next time. | I won't name it. I'll just draw it. | I know. I drew where the shade stops.
a : Alone. It wasn't far, once I'd drawn it. | Only mine. | #quietly#. The sun was very #hot#.

story a_story_shortcut [topic=memories|travel]
  : I drew a shortcut once over the dunes with #stick#. It looked shorter. It wasn't.
  : I walked it to be sure, and came back after dark with sand in everything.
  ask : Would you have turned back, or kept going?
  b : Turned back, I hope.
  b[stage=adult|old] : Kept going. We all do, at your age.
  : I kept going. Now I draw the long way and call it the short one.
